Z||000067||Mach10||09-06-2001||09:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>By FirstFiero:<BR><B>Their is harrasment where out in the world would only come into play if I continued after she told me to beat it. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Fair enough. <BR>Now ask yourself this: This is a family forum, Cliff would like to keep it that way. Is sexual harrassment a Good Thing to have on a family forum? Would you rather trumpet on about freedom of speech, or would you like to respect the fact that the comment was offensive to the party, and back off? How is your right to "free speech" more important than the feelings of another member who has done nothing (that I know of) to you? Just because it debases only one individual, does it make it any better than using a term like ni&&er, or ch1nk, or sp1nk? (Sorry cliff, I modified the terms so that the spyders wouldn't catch them. No reason to defame your sight while excersizing a socio-political debate)<P>I am truly sick of you self-righteous assholes who bleat on about freedom of speech. You taint the whole purpose for which the idea was born. Freedom of speech was created so that YOU could live your life how you wanted it, so that you wouldn't have to feel the burdon of oppression over your shoulders. Instead, you take it at face value, and consider it your god-given right to trample all over other people on the basis that you can say what you like. Know what? Racism and sexism are both forms of oppression, and are VERY rampant in your beloved United States. Free society indeed.<BR>Go ahead, ramble on about how you are allowed to say such things. But maybe, JUST MAYBE, consider that while you MAY say such things, you might consider excersizing your right not to say it, and lift some burden off another's shoulders.<BR>||||reg||1
